  "summary": "Justice Basheer Ahmed Sayeed College for Women in Teynampet, formerly S.I.E.T. Women's College, is maintained by the Southern India Education Trust founded by Justice Basheer Ahmed Sayeed and Mrs. Fathima Akhtar. The college's About page gives 1955 as its founding year (another college page says 1951). It began with 110 students and now has about 7,200, and it is affiliated to the University of Madras. It became autonomous in 2006 and is accredited A++ by NAAC. It runs a forenoon Shift I and an afternoon Shift II; Edugate lists the undergraduate programmes it has verified so far, without shift.",
